    "episode_id": 90943,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90943.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 21,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think it goes back to a thing that you started in this discussion, and that is being in the military, being that sort of, here's the rules, here's how you parse them out. If you don't like the rules, then you can either find a change rules, but as long as those are in place, that's what everybody should live by. There should be no two tiers of justice in our society. And coming is one who did not grow up on the quote. affluent side of the track or the, you know, the, the, the privilege side of the track, you know, working for it. That's very important to most everybody in America, no matter where you're from. And when I heard about this and that it's not, as you well know from federal law and for it, it's not a matter of, even in the law, did you intend, we're not even coming in intent on, did you have classified stuff on a private email server that by the way you hid forever and then the Department of Justice didn't even let the, the, uh, IT tech ever testify before Congress or turn over emails. I mean, again, you're starting to see this, this is toothed here because they were believing Hillary Clinton was going to be the next president. So all of this was a distraction. We needed to, they needed to keep it down. And it began to be a process where you said, I don't know, you really look at it and say, this is not right. Now, everybody needs to be, at least be honest about what was going on. So this started. Then you had this group. that, as you said, became part of the group that then began investigating the president, that then began to falsify Faisal warrants and move forward. And recently, John Durham's investigation is basically, I almost wish I could go back and put on the front of the cover instead of the Democrats' obsession with Donald Trump. He's like, we were right, see? Because we were, but nobody wanted to believe us because it goes back to that. So really, this whole book and the year that we discussed in depth in this book, the whole year of 2019 in particular, starts with a Clinton coverup. It starts with a trying to cover up or false over this email. And who is the center stage player? Jim Comey. Jim Comey steps up to that mic on in July of 2016 and makes this statement as a prosecutor. I'm sure made you and I know it deal with John Radcliffe and many others later on. Sort of say OK, what here? Because he said no regional prosecutor would make this case. And basically implying, you know, employing an attorney general at a time that was not strong enough to take advice and make those because they were already compromised. Remember the meeting on the tarmac with Bill Clinton. So it then just turns in to this, what we find out a little bit later, three weeks later, he had Peter Struck and these others who then began this process based on a Clinton directive through the Steele dossier to taint President Trump with the Russia connection. We now know this because documents were released later that this was even briefed to President Obama. You know, we now know that this was the tactic being used. But what is bad is you and I both think in political campaigns, political campaigns can run there. We run our narratives. You never expect the federal government at the highest level. to participate in it. And I think that's where this whole thing started. So yes, it goes back to 2016. The same people, the Peter strokes, the Jim Comey, the Andy McCabe, the James Bakers, all of them still tie into it. And what concerns me the most is it's not the regular federal agents. I've talked to so many in the FBI throughout. This was a group at the top, along with the intelligence community, that tied this narrative together, which led after President Trump was elected to try and cripple his first month. We remember that in 2017. And what bothers me the most, Kim, is that they knew this. And members of Congress began to know this dossier was falsified. It was never verified. Even Bruce Orr even said, look, there's problems with this dossier, but nobody would admit it because they were after one thing. They couldn't stand the fight that Hillary Clinton got beat.",
