  {
    "episode_id": 90943,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90943.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 33,
    "turn_text": "Well, it was it was concerning because that was all we were hearing during that time. It was it was going back and forth. And then when that happened and call me was fired and then you get the emails, you know, traffic and they're saying, let's don't waste this opportunity because when they they had the opportunity to say, okay, this has been a let's go ahead and appoint the special and mower was the one that came up and then you had an attorney general at the time, Jeff Sessions, who signed off on it because he had recused himself. People forget that, you know, not in the big picture, but he had sort of taken his hands off. So, in essence, the FBI was operating under Jim Comey as an entity unto itself, and this investigation was allowed to continue there. So, for me, it was a concern because we were at the time, and at the time, Trey Gowdy was, you know, Chairman, good luck. We're looking into this. This was beginning to be that buildup. But as soon as, and Ken, I don't know if you remember this, as soon as Mueller was named as the special prosecutor here. In the back of my mind, I said, you know, you could tell, this is what they were wanting, and then the Democrats just latched onto it as if it was a gospel. It just became, you know, you can't even speak ill of Robert Mueller at the time. And that's really where it began. And so, having all these same, you know, struck, McKay, you know, these, you know, or Paige, you know, all these names that became, you know, famous in that we were looking at, looking at the text messages, the emails, the insurance policies, all this kind of stuff. which was showed the bias here, then summed itself up into a very, well, turned out to be a very partisan investigation, but they missed one thing. When we talk about this, by the time the Mueller investigation all completed, by the time they had gained control of the House, which was about the time the Mueller investigation was rolling down, this was not the same Robert Mueller. And he had put around him some very partisan people that at the end of the day came back with what many of us knew, and that was the collusion wasn't there, and that there was not obstruction. But the Democrats couldn't take that. So really for me, that concerning part Even to this day, and one thing you, I don't know, I've talked about it in the book though, we're dealing with a FISA court. This is a secret court, and that's what it was supposed to be. And they were using it and manipulating this data again for a political narrative. That's not what we're about in America.",
