er won the chairmanship by saying I'm the one to impeach because he was part of the Clinton impeachment thing. Think about that. If you set your base up, your supporters up to say, we're going to get him. When you have a member of Congress who's sworn in for one day, basically saying, you know, I talked about my son and we talked about that. I'm going to impeach. We're going to impeach the something I word. I don't use it at all. You know, this guy, then there's no doubt about what they want to do. All they were trying to do was find something. The problem was Mueller came back. and was not what they wanted. And you remember those hearings. When we finally got Robert Mueller in July after we had to go through the show hearings and just, you know, excuse me, I remember that. I forgot something. Matt Whitaker. Matt Whitaker was the acting attorney general for all of three months and they were so scared that he had tampered or was messing with the Mueller investigation. We had to have him come in one week before Bill Barr took over. And Jerry Natter wouldn't have anything else he had to have him there. That's the mindset we were dealing",
