  {
    "episode_id": 90943,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90943.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 49,
    "turn_text": "Well, remember, one of the things I talked about in the book was we prepared for that hearing. You know, sometimes people think that Congress just runs off the, you know, sort of off the cup, but we didn't, we knew this was going to be a big hearing. We knew it was something in the narrative chain. So we had actually talked about it, practiced it. And if you want to get the book, we have one of our staffers, play Robert Mueller, very contentious tonight before, because for those of us who have been in rooms with Robert Mueller before, He was a very good law enforcement witness who was an attorney. He knew it. He would quickly answer your questions. He had command of his facts. He was always there. And then, and I make a mention of this, and it only happened to one of our members, Greg Stooby, who got what we determined was the Mueller stare. Because if Robert Mueller ever got to a point, and I had been in hearings two or three years earlier, where if he thought the member was being too cute, I guess, was maybe a way to put it. He would answer the question and say, I'm not saying any more, and he would just stare at the member, like, try me. And he knew it just, he was over. But when he walked in the room, and he read his open statement, Nadler then walked through his opening questions, which by the way, we're all scripted. I could have asked every Democrat, because I was sitting there reading him off Jerry's desk. And then when I started my questioning and I asked him about a simple issue of collusion and I'll end his report, right out of his report and he didn't have concept or control over his understanding, it told me this was going to be an entirely different Robert Mueller. And I think even today the Democrats will, some will acknowledge that that was true.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_06",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
