    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90943.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 62,
    "turn_text": "he was a new chairman and it was a very pressure packed time for a new chairman to be running a committee. There were a lot of procedural motions that we could prepare for for days that he wasn't prepared for because we surprised him with him. But you had also assembled, you and Chairman Goodlatte had assembled a really good group of people, people that had trial experience, people that, you know, the Jim Jordan's of the world, who are great orders. And with your leadership, really, I think when people looked at the Judiciary Committee, that wasn't the committee they wanted to put something in.",
