    "turn_text": "He was given an honest opinion in the press that won't hear it, and I think that was the problem. A funny story about that whole time. I wanted to have one more. The only thing I really tried to ever ask for in these hearings because we were, I mean we didn't have anything. I called one night and had Jerry Natalie actually hang up on me. He finally hung up and it was over this issue of could we have one more witness? I mean we're not, we know it's not fair but you have three or four, you could add more but give us at least one more and he hung up on me. But Turley presented it well if you remember the one of the issues that I think he pointed out very clearly because there was beginning, they didn't have They framed the impeachment as abuse of power over the phone call, but there's nothing criminal that they take a point to, so it's just this amorphous abuse of power. And then there's obstruction of Congress because he didn't do everything they wanted to do. And Jonathan Turley said, he said, if you go through with this, especially on the obstruction part, the only people that are guilty of obstruction is Congress.",
