  {
    "episode_id": 90943,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90943.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 85,
    "turn_text": "An airport or anywhere else. So I get wanted every single time. I walked through the magnetometer. We have, for the first time in the history of the House, a member who was not allowed to be served on committees for statements that she made before she got to Congress. We've had members impeached as federal judges who who then were elected to Congress and served and were allowed to serve on committees. We have people being kicked off of committees. We have the speaker for the first time ever in the history of the House deciding who the minority party can put on a special committee. She has denied the Republican conference the power to choose the members for the first time ever. We have all these new things happening that change the institution, in my view, degrade the institution. And yet, we look at this impeachment as sort of the kickoff for that kind of game.",
